{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The handbook (§29) enumerated only "},{"type":"text","value":"0","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" success · "},{"type":"text","value":"1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" other/network/timeout · "},{"type":"text","value":"2","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" usage/unknown command · "},{"type":"text","value":"3","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" auth · "},{"type":"text","value":"4","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" not-found · "},{"type":"text","value":"5","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" validation. This table keeps those six EXACTLY and adds "},{"type":"text","value":"6","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (conflict), "},{"type":"text","value":"7","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (rate-limited), "},{"type":"text","value":"8","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (server) as a strict superset — categories the handbook left folded into the generic bucket are now broken out without redefining any handbook code."}]},
